@@ -3674,4 +3674,54 @@
 <string id="timer_kanistra_bar_not_end"><text>Someone brought fuel to the Bar - you can charge your batteries.</text></string>
 <string id="timer_tm_kill_stalker_1_end"><text>The job with the trappers is cancelled.</text></string>
 <string id="new_info_pda_tip"><text>New information added to PDA</text></string>
+<string id="artmod_122_dialog_155"><text>Have you got a PDA instead of the watch or belt? You can have the gun.</text></string>
+<string id="artmod_122_dialog_156"><text>I have. I will fetch it, and two bottles as well. Thank you. Remember my friend.</text></string>
+<string id="artmod_122_dialog_157"><text>Wait, something does not add up. Let us leave the exchange for now.</text></string>
+<string id="esc_wolf_zone_info_dialog_50"><text>It is hard getting by here without a PDA. Where can I find a proper one?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_delayed"><text>Received late</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_delayed_body"><text>Message retained. The situation may have changed since it was sent.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_ask"><text>Sidorovich, have you got a PDA? A proper one, not somebody else's locked device.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_offer"><text>I have. Fifteen thousand. Before you start haggling: it is clean, it works, and it connects to the network. Search corpses if you want someone else's secrets. Come to me for working equipment.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_barman_ask"><text>Can I buy a PDA? I need one of my own.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_barman_offer"><text>I have a working one. Fifteen thousand, configured and fully charged. If you want it, I will check it here with you.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_base_accept"><text>All right. Fifteen thousand. I will take it.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_other_way"><text>Any cheaper way? Could someone rework an old one?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_vergas"><text>Show it to Vergas. He works on those if the electronics are intact. He does not work for free either. Ask him his price.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_unknown"><text>An old one might do. But I am not the one who will reflash it. Find a technician and make your arrangements with him.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_barman_vergas"><text>Ask Vergas. He works on other people's PDAs, provided they have not burnt out. Decide beforehand which ones you are willing to hand over.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_barman_unknown"><text>A used PDA can sometimes be reworked. You need a technician willing to do it. I do not do that work.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_not_now"><text>I will think about it. Not now.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_wait"><text>Agreed. Let me check the device, then we will settle up.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_barman_wait"><text>All right. Give me a moment to check it.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_no_deal"><text>Hold on. We cannot settle it like that. Check that you still have everything.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_upgrade_ask"><text>I heard you have some new PDAs. What makes them better?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_upgrade_offer"><text>I got a small batch. Twice the battery life, your own marks on the map, and a radiation readout if you have an active detector. Two second-tier artifacts for one. In suitable condition, of course.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_upgrade_accept"><text>That suits me. Take the two artifacts.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_ask"><text>Can you rework someone else's PDA for me?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_offer"><text>If its board has not burnt out. One device and a first-tier artifact, or five devices without an artifact: I can use the extras for parts. A discharged one is fine; I will charge it. But the records on anything you hand over will be lost.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_one"><text>One PDA and an artifact. Let us choose.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_five"><text>I will give you five PDAs. Let me pick them.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_choose"><text>Check the serial numbers. Mark the ones you want to hand over. Mark one again to remove it.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_choose_toggle"><text>Mark this one, or remove its mark.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_choose_next"><text>Show me the next one.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_confirm_donors"><text>I have chosen. You can have the marked ones.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_confirm"><text>Good. The list is in front of you. Once more: I do not preserve the records. Have you read everything you wanted from these PDAs?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_final_accept"><text>Yes. Go ahead.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_wait"><text>Then give me a moment to check the connection.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_donor_serial"><text>PDA serial</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_donor_charged"><text>charged</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_donor_empty"><text>discharged</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_donor_selected"><text>Marked:</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_artifact_payment"><text>Artifact payment:</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_selection_card"><text>Devices for reflashing</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_transaction_done"><text>PDA received and fully charged. Payment completed.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_transaction_failed"><text>The PDA could not be handed over. No payment was taken; your selected items remain yours.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_burn_ask"><text>My PDA burnt out in an emission. Have you got a replacement?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_sidor_burn_answer"><text>The simple ones are gone. And from what you tell me, another one might not last you long either. See Docent. He can find a new one or inspect the old one. Perhaps he can save your records.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_barman_burn_answer"><text>I have no ordinary ones left. Take the burnt device to Docent. He can tell you whether it is repairable or offer a replacement.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_burn_thanks"><text>Understood. I will speak to him.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_wolf_answer_known"><text>Ask Sidorovich, though he will want a fair amount of money. If you have used PDAs, show them to Vergas; he can rework them. And use your head when following an unfamiliar signal. The PDA will not think for you.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_wolf_answer_unknown"><text>Sidorovich sells them, but they are not cheap. Or find a technician who can rework a used one. Finding a PDA does not make it yours: it still has someone else's password and configuration.</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_poor_ask"><text>What is wrong with this artifact?</text></string>
+<string id="he_pda_vergas_poor_answer"><text>Look how little life it has left. I need it to power equipment, not sit on a shelf. Bring me one in better condition and we can talk.</text></string>
